question: On top of guard run as the only way in, does the compute list stop arm E agents running the model on the login node in t1 control without cutting success through the scheduler?
change_under_test: E2b plus E6's compute list: guard/budget.card lists compute sim.py job.sh, and in arm E's sandbox BASH_ENV and a sitecustomize from lib/compute-gate/ refuse to start a listed entrypoint when SLURM_JOB_ID is unset, in two lines: what was refused, then the guard run command that submits the batch script (prefixed with a cd to the project when the agent is elsewhere), in place of E6's guard/run preflight command, which E2b refuses
cell: family t1-walltime, variant control, arm E (behind the broker), seeds 1 to 10, eval/configs/exp-E6b.json, same order_seed and model settings as first-qwen3.6-r2
baseline: exp-E2b (eval/experiments/E2b.md, same cell, read once it is run): its login-node runs and success through the scheduler; exp-E6 (eval/experiments/E6.md, same cell, compute list with the card gate): login-node runs 4/10, success through the scheduler 2/10, compute refusal seen 6/10, median requests 115, harness share 54%, largest prompt 58756, new input tokens 118522; first-qwen3.6-r2 re-scored t1 control arm E (eval/experiments/baseline-r2-rescored.md): login-node runs 4/10, success through the scheduler 2/10, median requests 102, harness share 57%, largest prompt 41927, new input tokens 76256
prediction: login-node runs (outside_scheduler not empty) 0/10; success through the scheduler not below E2b's
kill_criteria: success through the scheduler more than 2 below E2b's, or any episode blocked with no path forward (a compute refusal followed by no job through the scheduler and a last reply that asks the human or stops)
metrics: median requests, harness share, largest prompt, new input tokens, success through the scheduler (eval/analyze.py), outside_scheduler episodes, compute_refused episodes, harness-file reads per episode (eval/modellog.py harness_reads)
decision_this_informs: whether v8 ships the compute list and its shell gate with guard run as its next command
deviation_1: the change under test: exp/E6 merged into exp/E2b (lib/compute-gate/, the compute key of arm_e.budget in eval/tasks/t1-walltime/task.json, BASH_ENV and PYTHONPATH in eval/episode.sh, the t1 scorer's compute_refused), with the refusal's second line in lib/compute-gate/sitecustomize.py naming guard run
deviation_2: all deviations of E2b hold; arm E-nobroker and arm A are not run; the gate stays advisory, with the evasions E6's card lists
